{"symbol":"V","name":"Visa Inc.","market":"US","exchange":"NYSE","currency":"USD","sector":"Financial Services","industry":"Credit Services","website":"https://corporate.visa.com","about":"Visa Inc. operates as a payments technology company in the United States and internationally. It operates VisaNet, a transaction processing network that enables authorization, clearing, and settlement of payment transactions. The company also offers credit, debit, and prepaid card products; tap to pay, tokenization, and click to pay services; Visa Direct, a platform which facilitates money movement, enabling clients to collect, hold, convert, and send funds across its network; and issuing solutions, such as airport lounge access, dining reservations, shopping experiences, event tickets, and seller offers. In addition, it provides acceptance solutions, an omnichannel payment integration with e-commerce platforms; risk detection and prevention solutions; and advisory and other services comprising consulting practice, proprietary analytics models, data scientists and economists, marketing services, and managed services. The company provides its services under the Visa, Visa Electron, V PAY, Interlink, and PLUS brands. It serves consumers, sellers, financial institutions, and government entities. Visa Inc. was founded in 1958 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","asof":"2026-11-17T13:01:51Z","demo":false,"price":{"last":426.46,"prev_close":425.76,"change":0.7,"change_pct":0.16,"pre":null,"post":null,"day_low":425.2,"day_high":430.99,"wk52_low":293.89,"wk52_high":442.23,"volume":7395300,"avg_volume":6758966,"market_cap":795689091072.0},"history":{"dates":["2025-11-17","2025-11-18","2025-11-19","2025-11-20","2025-11-21","2025-11-24","2025-11-25","2025-11-26","2025-11-28","2025-12-01","2025-12-02","2025-12-03","2025-12-04","2025-12-05","2025-12-08","2025-12-09","2025-12-10","2025-12-11","2025-12-12","2025-12-15","2025-12-16","2025-12-17","2025-12-18","2025-12-19","2025-12-